---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show a run's metadata: id, status, timestamps, launcher, and description.

Two fields report time and they mean different things. Duration is the workload
length requested at launch. Elapsed is wall-clock time, which also spans
provisioning, setup and teardown, so the two legitimately differ. Source is the
`antithesis.source` the run was launched from, when the launcher recorded one.
User-defined attributes (`attrs.<name>` params at launch) are listed under
Attributes. The `vcs.*` parameters that the Antithesis GitHub trigger action
records (repository, branch, and commit) are listed under Version Control.

Incomplete runs also show the failure moment (Failure Hash/VTime) to pass to
`runs logs`, and the Failure Reason when the run reports one. `web` opens the
triage report in a browser.

Examples:
  snouty runs show <run_id>
  snouty runs show <run_id> --web

Add --json for machine-readable output. The run prints as one JSON object. With
`web` it prints the report URL as {"url": ...} and opens no browser:
  snouty --json runs show <run_id> | jq -r .status

Usage: snouty runs show [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
  -w, --web
          Open the run's triage report in a browser instead of printing details

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
